Common Waste Water and Waste Gas Treatment/Management Systems in the Chemical Sector, BREF CWW (@ic-water-waste: 0, is #reference, #part-of @ic-sources) { r_3DD06XBCANC091G38HBZ4BX7Y9
European Commission, Joint Research Centre. Common Waste Water and Waste Gas Treatment/Management Systems in the Chemical Sector, BREF CWW. published January 2017; BAT conclusions June 2016. [Official reference and full-text access](https://bureau-industrial-transformation.jrc.ec.europa.eu/reference/common-waste-water-and-waste-gas-treatmentmanagement-systems-chemical-sector-0).

This full systems reference develops water saving, collection, management and treatment of wastewater/sludge and residuals, with gas, diffuse-emission and other site topics in its stated edition.

Read the complete management, inventory, characterization, collection and treatment sequence used by the process account. Distinguish preventing a constituent, recovering it and transferring it between air, water and solid streams. Read later WGC material for its newer detailed air-treatment scope rather than confusing the report and conclusions dates.

Identity, stated scope, date and official access were checked on 29 October 2026. This is a dated technical reference, not a claim that every described plant, technology or legal reference is current everywhere. Preserve its attribution, actual reuse notice and third-party exceptions; public access is not described as a blanket CC licence. Full-text or automated inspection limits are distinguished where relevant. No book, figure, industrial data or associated media is bundled.

